1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,017
Welcome to Module four!

2
00:00:02,017 --> 00:00:05,380
In this lesson, we'll tour
the Conversations inbox,

3
00:00:05,380 --> 00:00:08,347
where every message from
every channel lands.

4
00:00:08,347 --> 00:00:11,249
By the end, you'll know
how to find, filter,

5
00:00:11,249 --> 00:00:14,150
star and assign any
conversation in seconds.

6
00:00:15,002 --> 00:00:17,347
Click Conversations in the sidebar.

7
00:00:17,347 --> 00:00:19,157
This is your unified inbox.

8
00:00:19,157 --> 00:00:22,976
Texts, emails, WhatsApp,
Facebook and Instagram messages,

9
00:00:22,976 --> 00:00:26,059
website chats and phone
calls all arrive here,

10
00:00:26,059 --> 00:00:29,811
so nobody on your team has
to check five different apps.

11
00:00:30,663 --> 00:00:32,292
The screen has three parts.

12
00:00:32,292 --> 00:00:34,826
On the left is your list of conversations.

13
00:00:34,826 --> 00:00:38,747
In the middle is the full thread
with the person you've selected.

14
00:00:38,747 --> 00:00:41,341
And on the right are
their contact details,

15
00:00:41,341 --> 00:00:43,815
so you always know who you're talking to.

16
00:00:44,666 --> 00:00:48,516
Each row shows the contact, a
preview of the last message,

17
00:00:48,516 --> 00:00:50,374
and how long ago it arrived.

18
00:00:50,374 --> 00:00:55,751
The small badge on the photo shows the
channel: green for a text, blue for email,

19
00:00:55,751 --> 00:00:57,012
pink for Instagram.

20
00:00:57,012 --> 00:00:59,999
Rows in bold, with a
blue number, are unread.

21
00:01:00,849 --> 00:01:02,853
Click a conversation to open it.

22
00:01:02,853 --> 00:01:07,676
This one starts with a missed call from
a new number, then an automatic text,

23
00:01:07,676 --> 00:01:08,741
then their reply.

24
00:01:08,741 --> 00:01:12,437
Opening it marks it as read,
so the blue number disappears.

25
00:01:12,437 --> 00:01:17,698
Every message with this person, on every
channel, stays together in this one thread.

26
00:01:18,548 --> 00:01:20,576
Across the top are four views.

27
00:01:20,576 --> 00:01:23,482
Unread shows only what
still needs a reply.

28
00:01:23,482 --> 00:01:25,781
Recents shows the latest activity.

29
00:01:25,781 --> 00:01:28,958
Starred holds the
conversations you've flagged.

30
00:01:28,958 --> 00:01:31,526
And All shows everything, however old.

31
00:01:32,376 --> 00:01:35,236
To find something fast,
use the search box.

32
00:01:35,236 --> 00:01:38,961
You can search by name, or
by words inside the messages.

33
00:01:38,961 --> 00:01:43,151
Here, typing "whitening" finds
everyone who has asked about it.

34
00:01:44,001 --> 00:01:46,833
The filter button
narrows the list further.

35
00:01:46,833 --> 00:01:51,442
You can show only conversations
assigned to you, only unassigned ones,

36
00:01:51,442 --> 00:01:52,759
or a single channel.

37
00:01:52,759 --> 00:01:57,566
Let's find the unassigned conversations,
because those have no owner yet.

38
00:01:58,418 --> 00:02:02,423
Ava asked on Instagram about
whitening for sensitive teeth.

39
00:02:02,423 --> 00:02:06,835
Open the conversation, click the
assign button, and choose Priya,

40
00:02:06,835 --> 00:02:08,532
our whitening specialist.

41
00:02:08,532 --> 00:02:12,944
Priya is notified, and her photo
now appears on the conversation.

42
00:02:13,792 --> 00:02:16,355
Star conversations you
want to come back to,

43
00:02:16,355 --> 00:02:19,209
like a patient who's still
deciding on treatment.

44
00:02:19,209 --> 00:02:23,577
And if you've read something but can't
deal with it yet, mark it as unread,

45
00:02:23,577 --> 00:02:25,033
so it stays on your list.

46
00:02:25,890 --> 00:02:31,185
On the right, you see the contact's details,
tags, opportunities and appointments,

47
00:02:31,185 --> 00:02:32,864
without leaving the inbox.

48
00:02:32,864 --> 00:02:36,802
Olivia is an open Invisalign
lead, and she hasn't booked yet,

49
00:02:36,802 --> 00:02:39,643
so she's a perfect
person to reply to first.

50
00:02:39,643 --> 00:02:42,420
Click View contact to
open her full record.

51
00:02:43,273 --> 00:02:44,304
Here's a pro tip.

52
00:02:44,304 --> 00:02:49,219
Agree on one rule with your team: every
new conversation gets assigned within the

53
00:02:49,219 --> 00:02:49,522
hour.

54
00:02:49,522 --> 00:02:54,436
Then each person uses the Assigned to me
filter, so they only see their own work,

55
00:02:54,436 --> 00:02:56,681
and nothing slips through the cracks.

56
00:02:57,537 --> 00:02:58,895
That's your inbox tour!

57
00:02:58,895 --> 00:03:03,797
In the next lesson, you'll learn to reply
on every channel, from one single thread.

58
00:03:03,797 --> 00:03:04,623
See you there.
